---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Font Finder"
  description="Read the terms of service governing the use of the Font Finder website and typography tools."
>
  <article class="py-12 sm:py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-muted border border-border text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground mb-4">
        <span>Legal Terms</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-foreground tracking-tight">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Last revised: March 2026.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
      
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight">
          1. Agreement to Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using Font Finder (the "Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you disagree with any part of the terms, you may discontinue use of the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight">
          2. Permitted Use
        </h2>
        <p>
          Font Finder is provided free of charge for identifying typography, inspecting letterform specimens, and obtaining open-source font resources. You agree not to misuse the service or attempt to disrupt its infrastructure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight">
          3. Font Licensing & Intellectual Property
        </h2>
        <p>
          The font families cataloged and verified through this service are distributed under their respective open-source licenses, primarily the SIL Open Font License (OFL) or Apache 2.0 license. Users are responsible for adhering to the specific license terms of any font downloaded or embedded in production systems.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight">
          4. Disclaimer of Warranties
        </h2>
        <p>
          The Service is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. While we strive for extreme optical precision and verify all fonts against official Google Fonts registries, we make no warranties that identification results will be 100% error-free in all low-resolution or distorted image scenarios.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
